# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Particle event LOCLPAR0003, 600 s, in 13 pieces (one component each) built at the attitude of their
# time span (yaw change <= 10 deg per piece); together they make up the event.

# Piece 1 of 13: 0-232.881 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/50 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 780 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw -68.66 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source LOCLPAR0003_p1
LOCLPAR0003_p1.ParticleType 3
LOCLPAR0003_p1.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction LOCLPAR0003_p1_beam.dat
LOCLPAR0003_p1.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835960700.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curves (absolute unix times): LOCLPAR0003_p1_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p2_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p3_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p4_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p5_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p6_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p7_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p8_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p9_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p10_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p11_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p12_lightcurve.dat, LOCLPAR0003_p13_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
LOCLPAR0003_p1.Lightcurve File false LOCLPAR0003_p1_lightcurve_shifted.dat

